<title>FRANCE: French industry sees workforce fall in Q2 - survey.</title>
<headline>French industry sees workforce fall in Q2 - survey.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French industry heads expect staffing levels to fall further in the second quarter, but at a slower pace than in the first quarter, according to a quarterly survey by national statistics institute INSEE.</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following data, seasonally adjusted unless stated:</p>
<p>					 Apr 97  Jan 97 Oct 96 Jul 96</p>
<p>Past trend</p>
<p> Total industry			-21    -22    -22    -18</p>
<p> Manufacturing industry (unadj)  -25    -28    -22    -12</p>
<p>Future trend</p>
<p> Total industry (unadj)	    -16    -23    -29    -20</p>
<p> Manufacturing industry (unadj)  -18    -23    -31    -20</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
